      "content": "Hey, I'm seeing a bunch of denials on our recent dermatological claims for \"atypical skin presentations.\" Specifically, we're having trouble with how to differentiate between various irregular pigment patterns and unusual texture anomalies when the morphology doesn't fit a standard diagnosis. Can you walk me through the hierarchy for coding these types of irregular or anomalous skin features in ICD-10? We need to make sure the specificity is high enough to avoid the \"unspecified\" bucket.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
